World "DFA"
Title "Deterministic Automata"

Introduction "
A **deterministic finite automaton** is the simplest kind of computer: finitely
many states, no memory beyond the current state, and one fixed move for each
symbol it reads.

In this world you'll run machines, check what they accept, refute false claims,
and finally prove *exactly* which language a machine recognises.
"
